(c) Studied only — no code taken

Each item below was studied, and no code was taken from it. Do not
mistake these influences for vendored code.

1. CLIProxyAPI (github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI,
   commit 90c447d3a8727d115aa7552ec93ce023736ed492) — plugin
   loader/ABI pattern and plugin config toggles:
   studied, no code taken. License name: MIT.
2. cronet-go opt-in design — the evaluated TLS-engine option of a
   future `with_cronet` build flavour plus a hash-verified sidecar;
   studied, no code taken. (The cronet-go library itself is listed
   in (b) as graph-only.)
3. muse-cli 0.6.1 behavioral reference
   (github.com/thoitiettxl-cyber/muse-cli) — differential reference
   for gateway framing, the exit-code/JSON contract, Telegram caps,
   and node-ID rules; behavior reimplemented:
   studied, no code taken.
   (The byte-identical descriptor assets are listed in (a).)
   License name: MIT.
4. Noise protocol, XX pattern — the public Noise specification's
   handshake pattern, as implemented through the flynn/noise library
   listed in (b); studied, no code taken; no specification text
   copied. License name: not applicable (specification, not code).
5. SB-T (github.com/thoitiettxl-cyber/SB-T,
   commit c03b73d6577505c5e1e947d760a8b0638202cab5) — former
   KernelSU module WebUI pattern: the `box.webui` JSON
   envelope shape, the `box.want` desired-state marker
   semantics, the vendored on-disk dashboard
   (`dashboard.path = "ui"`), and the `kernelsu` exec-bridge
   call pattern: studied and adapted (reimplemented in the
   former `module/scripts/castctl-ctl` and
   `module/webroot/index.html`, removed with the module), no
   SB-T code taken, with stated divergences (boot gating on
   the want marker, single-file webroot, UI preservation via
   explicit update). License name: Apache-2.0. Full mapping
   in docs/provenance.md §12.
